 "verdict": "NOT SUPPORTED, BUT NOT CONTRADICTED EITHER -- no gradient. None of the predicted blocks varies monotonically with distance (CTCF flat, promoter flat, Pol II flat), so the data does not distinguish a short-range occupancy mechanism from a distance-independent one. Two specifics worth keeping: the promoter block contributes most in the <10 kb stratum (+0.0309, its largest of any stratum), which is the TF half of the hypothesis; while element Pol II contributes essentially nothing at any distance (-0.0023, +0.0028, -0.0004, -0.0079), so the polymerase-allocation half is specifically unsupported. The largest block everywhere is competition, which is neither occupancy nor contact."
